,{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A maximum flow from ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"sink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": highest-label push–relabel with the gap and global","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relabelling heuristics (Goldberg–Tarjan; Cherkassky–Goldberg), in two phases as LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Preflow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (NetworkX’s default ","type":"text"},{"code":"preflow_push","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Boost ","type":"text"},{"code":"push_relabel_max_flow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). O(n² √m).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Which maximum flow is returned is unspecified; ","type":"text"},{"code":"value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumCut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are not.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/maximumflow(from:to:capacity:)","title":"maximumFlow(from:to:capacity:)"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/minimumCut(capacity:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Flows3CutV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Cut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"minimumCut(capacity:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumCut(capacity:)","url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumcut(capacity:)","abstract":[{"text":"A minimum cut over all nonempty proper vertex sets S, by the capacity of the edges leaving","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"S (igraph ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mincut()"},{"text":" on a directed graph): Hao and Orlin’s algorithm (LEMON ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HaoOrlin"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one push–relabel run that moves the sink through every vertex, then the same on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reversed graph, so both the cuts with the first vertex on the source side and those with it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the sink side are seen. Which minimum cut is returned when several exist is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified, but the same input always gives the same cut. nil below two vertices.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"text":" is called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n²m) in the worst case.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/minimumVertexCut()":{"title":"minimumVertexCut()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumVertexCut()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A minimum vertex cut, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, by Even’s pair order 